nned Actions: checkout7.0.1, mise-action5.0.1, configure-pages6, upload-pages-artifact5, deploy-pages5.0.1 and upload-artifact7.0.1. Preserve the complete gate, runtime versions, exact-tree artifact trust, main-only serialized publishing and bounded retention.\n\nIndependent clean-context code and adversarial reviewers approve the bounded App implementation and unchanged migration workflow scope. A previous-source normal-motion native-frame/keyboard control loses target focus and retains UTC; the candidate retains CST ambiguity and recovers the exact Tokyo result. All fifteen core case/profile combinations passed first attempts. Complementary ownership/request probes and their retained QA setup corrections are recorded. Physical/OS focus and the historical untraced Linux fill sequence remain qualified.\n\nThe prior held gate37288000068 was green after one failed first attempt and a successful retry. Its first-failure screenshot/context and successful-retry trace are distinct. Actual v7 timing and flaky-success diagnostic uploads were verified on unchanged workflow bytes. The new final exact-head gate runs ordinary mode without timing instrumentation, followed by artifact/public-byte audit, hosted offline and matching focus interaction checks, an explicit draft-preserving update, and one complete manual publishing fallback. These final delivery checks are pending.\n\nOriginal briefs, source identities, attempt reconciliation, environment/clocks and separate implementation/report verdicts: docs/qa/actions-upgrade-2026-10-05 and docs/qa/copy-focus-2026-10-05. Deployment deadline/cancellation and historical rollback remain unexercised. TIE-370's unidentified historical cause remains open. TIE-375's ≥20% complete-pair quota/storage plus faster raw-time target remains unmet; no monthly savings claim.\n\nTracks [TIE-376](https://linear.app/tienlam/issue/TIE-376/modernize-pinned-ci-actions-and-verify-both-publishing-paths) and [TIE-377](https://linear.app/tienlam/issue/TIE-